13369	{"artifactId":"LLD-dd277f9cddd6d879-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-dd277f9cddd6d879-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T19:00:08.290Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The upstream intent (triage rationale: BUILD joins the pending scan; its document must be servable to the review pane; a decision goes through the existing approve path with its code-review rule; no plugin source change) is fully designed, and nothing beyond it is built.","evidence":"LLD-dd277f9cddd6d879-s1.json meta.triageRationale names exactly these three points. The design covers each: PENDING_KINDS + CR-presence condition (2.1), the marker/exists check so only a servable BUILD.md path is offered, and approve/reject through handleReviewDecision -> approveWorkflowTarget. handleArtifactContent (artifact-content.ts:164-244) has no kind filter, so a BUILD .md with a marker is served as-is; no plugin source is changed. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-dd277f9cddd6d879-s1.json, src/workflow/artifact-content.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today PENDING_KINDS is SPEC/DEF/HLD/LLD/PLAN/ISSUE/CR, the scan makes one readdirSync, skips a malformed file with a log, and treats pending as neither approvedAt nor rejectedAt.","evidence":"pending.ts:39 `PENDING_KINDS = ['SPEC', 'DEF', 'HLD', 'LLD', 'PLAN', 'ISSUE', 'CR']`; :110 single `readdirSync(dir).filter(...)` with no sort; :118-123 try/catch + log.warn + continue; :127-128 the two stamp checks. [files: src/workflow/pending.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Approving a BUILD record whose Story's code review is missing, unreadable or by the same party is withheld into skipped[] under any configuration; a block verdict withholds only when codeReview.enforce is on.","evidence":"gates.ts:686-725 otherPartyReviewGap: for a BUILD- id it reads CR-<epicHash>-<storyId>.json via readJsonOrUndefined and returns a gap when undefined ('Completion requires a code review of this Story, and none has been run') or when reviewer === author; approveArtifactByJsonPath throws ReviewBlockedError (:621-625), which approveWorkflowTarget routes to skipped (:868-869), independent of enforce. code-review/gate.ts:102-112: with enforce off a block is returned as advisory warn and 'NEVER withholds completion'. Note: for a malformed CR file the relayed reason says none was run, not 'unreadable', and a CR that parses but has no meta is not withheld; neither changes the design's outcome. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts]","action":"None required. Optionally word the malformed-CR reason as the message the gate actually gives.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A rejected build record stays rejected across later validates, the pane's decision call refuses a further decision on it, and approving in the chat clears the rejection.","evidence":"standalone-record.ts:424-428 mergeWithPrior: 'a later validate must never clobber a completed (or rejected) story', prior rejectedAt/rejectReason re-spread. review-decision.ts:149-153 returns `cannot ${decision} ... it is already ${state}, not awaiting review` for a non-pending record. gates.ts:650-652 approveArtifactByJsonPath: 'Clear any prior rejection if we're re-approving' deletes rejectedAt and rejectReason. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts, src/workflow/review-decision.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"deriveMdPath already resolves a BUILD record's BUILD.md, and the content and decision calls already serve a BUILD record by that path when the file carries the artifact marker.","evidence":"path-scheme.ts:48 ArtifactKind includes 'BUILD' and :70 STORY_SCOPED includes 'BUILD'; pending.ts:188 deriveMdPath takes any ArtifactKind. Both handleArtifactContent (artifact-content.ts:199) and handleReviewDecision (review-decision.ts:131) resolve the json through jsonPathForMd, which throws without a marker (gates.ts:1017-1026) - the reason the design adds the marker check. The build writer puts the marker on the first line (standalone-record.ts:331), so the 512-character window finds it; jsonPathForMd itself reads 4096 characters, so the design's window is narrower but sufficient for writer-produced files. [files: src/workflow/path-scheme.ts, src/workflow/pending.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts]","action":"None required. Consider using the same 4096-character window as readArtifactIdMarker so the two never disagree.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The VS Code plugin passes kind through as a string and its table already ranks BUILD between ISSUE and CR, so no plugin source changes.","evidence":"docs-review-list.ts:22 `RV_KINDS=['SPEC','DEF','HLD','LLD','PLAN','ISSUE','BUILD','CR']`; the type select builds its options from the kinds present (:49-54). docs-review-client.ts:125 `kind: a.kind` with no enumeration; :122 and :139 skip an empty mdPath, matching the design's pathless handling. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-list.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-client.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No consumer of PendingKind / PENDING_KINDS / listPendingArtifacts exists outside pending.ts and the two test files the inventory names, and pending.test.ts:94 is the test whose title becomes false.","evidence":"Grep over *.ts/*.kt: PendingKind and PENDING_KINDS occur only in src/workflow/pending.ts; listPendingArtifacts is imported only by pending.test.ts and artifact-kinds.test.ts; handleWorkflowPending is used by src/daemon/index.ts and pending.test.ts. pending.test.ts:94 is 'listPendingArtifacts excludes a non-union KIND even when unapproved (BUILD)' with a BUILD fixture and no CR. [files: src/workflow/pending.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/pending.test.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"artifact-kinds.test.ts seeds an unapproved BUILD with a CR record and a marker-carrying BUILD.md, so its pending result gains one BUILD row while its lower bound and before/after comparison still hold.","evidence":"artifact-kinds.test.ts:58 seeds BUILD-<HASH>-s1 unapproved, :65 CR-<HASH>-s1, :66-67 writes S001/BUILD.md with artifactIdMarker(BUILD-<HASH>-s1) under docs/epics/pay-things-E20260115abc123de, the folder the record's createdAt derives. :112 asserts `length >= 4`; :131 compares readAll before and after adding a TESTS record, and TESTS is not a pending kind, so the BUILD row is identical on both sides. [files: src/workflow/__tests__/artifact-kinds.test.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"At the end of a chat turn that runs the code review the presenter opens the BUILD record first and the CR record last, so the code review is the document on show.","evidence":"review-presenter.ts:142-147 opens every newly pending document in the list's order, so with a sorted scan BUILD-<x> is opened before CR-<x>; that part is true. I did not read docsReviewHost.openArtifact to confirm the last quiet open is the one left on show, and review-presenter.ts:128-135 opens a document at once when a tool result carries pendingApproval.artifactPath: if the code review's result presents the CR that way, the CR is opened mid-turn and the BUILD record is opened last at the turn's end. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/review-presenter.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"Confirm which document is left on show when the CR is presented by a tool result during the turn, and state it in the edge case (or pin it in the plugin test).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"change-sites.4","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The JetBrains plugin reads the same list and has no enumeration of pending kinds, so a BUILD row is carried by its kind text.","evidence":"DaemonGateway.kt:866 pendingArtifacts forwards workflow.pending; a grep of jetbrains-plugin/src/main for the quoted kind names (SPEC/DEF/HLD/LLD/PLAN/ISSUE/CR) finds none; ReviewToolWindow.kt:196 and :223 only print `dto.kind` / `value.kind`. [files: jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/DaemonGateway.kt, jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/review/ReviewToolWindow.kt]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Nothing stored changes; in this repository the list grows by at most 7 build records, and older build records without epicCreatedAt exist and must be handled as pathless.","evidence":"Glob finds 146 .insrc/artifacts/BUILD-*.json; 139 of them contain approvedAt or rejectedAt, leaving 7 unstamped. Only 70 of the 146 carry epicCreatedAt (standalone-record.ts:70-73: 'Absent on older records'), so the older shape the design guards against is real. The design adds no field and writes nothing: the scan stays read-only. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts, src/workflow/pending.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A BUILD record and its Story's CR record share the identical file-name suffix, including lower-case epic story ids, so a set lookup on CR-<x>.json is the same record the approval gate reads.","evidence":"storage.ts:160-161 buildArtifactId = `BUILD-${epicHash}-${storyId}` and :173-174 codeReviewArtifactId = `CR-${epicHash}-${storyId}`; gates.ts:696 and code-review/gate.ts:72 build the CR path with the same function from the BUILD's own epicHash and storyId. The store holds matching pairs in both forms (BUILD-/CR-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s1, BUILD-/CR-008e146ad1475ef9-s1). [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A withheld approval comes back from handleReviewDecision as outcome 'withheld' with the approve call's reason and stamps nothing, and an unreadable store or one malformed file behaves as today.","evidence":"review-decision.ts:164-171: when res.approved is empty, `outcome = 'withheld'; reason = res.skipped[0]?.reason ?? 'the approval was not recorded'`; approveWorkflowTarget pushes to skipped without calling the stamp (gates.ts:855-857, 868-869). pending.ts:76-80 maps a thrown scan to `{ error }`, and :118-123 skips a malformed file. The CR is checked by name only, so a malformed CR file cannot throw inside the scan. [files: src/workflow/review-decision.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/pending.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion maps to a test that can be written against existing seams: ac1 and ac2 to the listPendingArtifacts unit subjects, ac3 to the content and decision integration subjects, with the withheld case through the decision handler's approve seam.","evidence":"The acceptance mapping lists proving tests for ac1, ac2 and ac3. The seam the ac3 withheld case needs exists: review-decision.ts:86-89 ReviewDecisionDeps.approve (`typeof approveWorkflowTarget`) used at :164. pending.test.ts:37-46 has the temporary-store fixture the unit subjects reuse, and artifact-kinds.test.ts:66-67 shows the marker-carrying BUILD.md fixture pattern the path subject needs. [files: src/workflow/review-decision.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/pending.test.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/artifact-kinds.test.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":14,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-13T19:00:08.290Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
